 {
  "ref": "314.16(A)",
  "edition": "2023",
  "status": "VERIFIED-2023",
  "source": "N3 PI 3972 (base text)",
  "text": "The volume of a wiring enclosure (box) shall be the total volume of the assembled sections and, where used, the space provided by plaster rings, domed covers, extension rings, and so forth, that are marked with their volume or are made from boxes the dimensions of which are listed in Table 314.16(A).",
  "subsections_2023": [
   {
    "item": "(1)",
    "title": "Standard Boxes",
    "text": "The volumes of standard boxes that are not marked with their volume shall be as given in Table 314.16(A)."
   },
   {
    "item": "(2)",
    "title": "Other Boxes",
    "text": "Boxes 1650 cm3 (100 in.3) or less, other than those described in Table 314.16(A), and nonmetallic boxes shall be durably and legibly marked by the manufacturer with their volume(s). Boxes described in Table 314.16(A) that have a volume larger than is designated in the table shall be permitted to have their volume marked as required by this section."
   }
  ],
